**HUNT THE WUMPUS PROTOCOL** (HTWP)

# OVERVIEW
The Hunt The Wumpus Protocol (HTWP) is a tet-based communication protocol
used by clients and servers to run a multiplayer Hunt the Wumpus game. 

The protocol is inspired by both HTTP and SMTP. 

From HTTP, HTWP borrows the idea of structured messages consisting of: 
- Start line
- Headers 
- Optional message body

From HTTP, HTWP borrows the idea of a server and client using responses
and requests to communicate. Players will recieve responses from server 
when request is made or something happens in game. 

From SMTP, HTWP borrows the idea of using simple four letter text commands
and response codes. 

This hybrid approach allows HTWP messages to contain all the useful informantion
in a structured but easy to read format. 

# BEHAVIOR: 
communcation between a client and server works like this: 
* A player (client) sends request using simple commands to server
* The server responds with status codes and messages
* The server may also send event updates when something happends during a game

All messages are plain text and separated by \r\n 

# FORMAT: 
========================================================
                    HTWP REQUEST
========================================================
START-LINE
+-------------------+-------------+----------------------+
| 4 Letter COMMAND  | [Argument]  | Game Version         |
|                   |             | (HTWP/1.0)           |
+-------------------+-------------+----------------------+
HEADERS
+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Header: Value                                         |
| Header: Value                                         |
| Header: Value                                         |
| Header: Value                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Blank Space                                           |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
BODY (optional)
+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Any additional information is put here                |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

========================================================
                    HTWP RESPONSE
========================================================
START-LINE
+----------------------+--------------+------------------+
| Game Version         | STATUS CODE  | STATUS MESSAGE   |
| (HTWP/1.0)           |              |                  |
+----------------------+--------------+------------------+
HEADERS
+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Header: Value                                         |
| Header: Value                                         |
| Header: Value                                         |
| Header: Value                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Blank Space                                           |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
BODY (optional)
+-------------------------------------------------------+
| Any additional information is put here                |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

# SOCKET CONFIG: 
Host: thomas.butler.edu 
Port: 52805
Type: TCP

# CLIENT COMMANDS:
Players interact with server using four letter commands
| Command   | Description                                 |
| --------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| JOIN      | Join the server                             |
| QUIT      | Quit the server                             |
| PLAY      | Join a game                                 |
| EXIT      | Leave a game                                |
| MOVE X    | Move to cave number X                       |
| FIRE X    | Fire an arrow into cave X                   |
| HELP      | Display available commands                  |
| TALK name | Send a private message to a player          |
| YELL      | Send a message to everyone in the same cave |


# CODES:
Server response are grouped by category

200 series -- Successful
200 - OK
201 - joined server 
202 - joined game

400 series -- Game Events 
405 - eaten by wumpus
406 - fell into pit
407 - picked up by bats 
408 - Arrow hit wumpus 
409 - Arrow missed
410 - another player eaten by wumpus 
411 - player entered cave
412 - Player killed wumpus
413 - Player has yelled to everyone
414 - player is talking with you

600 series -- Errors 
600 - Unable to join server 
601 - Unable to join game 
602 - invalid cave number 
603 - No arrows left 
604 - invalid command

# HEADERS:
The following headers may appear in HTWP messages

| Header       | Type      | Description            |
| ------------ | --------- | ---------------------- |
| Host         | string    | server hostname        |
| Port         | int       | server port            |
| Player       | string    | player name            |
| Game-ID      | string    | game identifier        |
| Date         | string    | timestamp              |
| Current-Cave | int       | player's location      |
| Nearby-Caves | list<int> | adjacent caves         |
| Message      | boolean   | indicates chat message |

# DESIGN DECISIONS: 
text-based protocol 
HTWP is fully text based to make it easy to debug, readable, and compatible
with tools like netcat

HTTP-Style structure
Using start lines and headers allows messages to carry large amounts of structured 
information without becoming confusing. 

Four letter Commands 
Commands were limited to four letters to keep the protocol consistent, easy to parse, 
and easy for players to remember 

Response codes
using numeric codes allows easy error handing. Clients will be able to easily interprete 
what the response code is. Because the codes are numeric they can be seperated into 
successes, errors, and events. 
